Umia Protocol — licensing overview

These contracts are licensed per file. The SPDX identifier on line 1 of each
source file is the source of truth; this file is a map, not a grant. Full
texts are in licenses/.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

    BUSL-1.1  The implemented protocol mechanism: markets, settlement,
              governance, launchpad, hook, and vaults. Non-production use is
              unrestricted; production use is subject to the Additional Use
              Grant in licenses/BUSL_LICENSE. Converts to MIT on 2030-08-11.

    MIT       The integration surface: src/interfaces/**, the shared type
              libraries, and generic math. Build against Umia freely.

    MIT       Reclaim-derived Umia verifier and helpers in src/zktls/**.

    MIT       abi/ — contract ABIs are free to use.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

See README.md for the full map; `bash check-licenses.sh` enforces it in CI.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses. MetaVesT (AGPL-3.0) is used
only by tests and deployment scripts; production contracts declare minimal local
interfaces instead of importing it.

Copyright (c) 2026 Umia S.P., a segregated portfolio of Umia Launcher S.P.C.
Trademarks are not licensed by any of the above.
